```java
void process(Lock lock) {
    lock.lock();
    try {
        riskyCall();          // may throw
    } finally {
        lock.unlock();        // ALWAYS released, even on exception
    }
    // No catch here: the caller decides how to handle the failure.
}
```
*The exception from `riskyCall()` still propagates — `finally` only guarantees the unlock happens first.*

